# Cargo build output. This is regenerated by `cargo build` and is never worth
# reviewing: it contains absolute paths and a copy of every dependency.
target/

# Cargo.lock is committed on purpose. This is a library and an executable, and
# the lock file is what makes a build on another machine the same build. Its
# presence here means the earlier commit that added it without a .gitignore was
# not wrong, only badly ordered.